    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "458004c2-2f2b-40bf-8fd7-cad968995e49",
      "key": "9c1d8a44-6419-4fc0-972b-beb3f2a002bb",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "cccec8a9-a0ae-4e51-9f73-fd69aada68f2",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide in Kent\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "08a2c371-676b-47d9-9e66-a2c209cf0955",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on a half board basis at the 3* Best Western Abbots Barton Hotel. Located a fifteen minute walk from the centre of Canterbury, facilities at the hotel include a restaurant and bar and all rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "d36cb814-ed12-4983-9647-04c8d864a7bf",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHever Castle \u0026amp; Gardens\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EUNESCO listed Canterbury - guided tour\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECanterbury Cathedral\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELeeds Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESissinghurst Castle Garden\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGreat Dixter House \u0026amp; Gardens\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll Saints\u2019 Church, Tudeley\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDover Castle \u0026amp; Secret Wartime Tunnels\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWalmer Castle\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIghtham Mote\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "e220d5fe-47de-4e63-864e-29bbeada80fd",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EChartwell - the family home of Sir Winston Churchill from 1924, the rooms remain much as they were when he lived there\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EKent Battle of Britain Museum - the most comprehensive and longest serving Battle of Britain museum in the United Kingdom\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETurner Contemporary Gallery, Margate - showcases a changing range of art and artists, both historical and contemporary, with at least one work by Turner at all times which may be a painting, sketch or sketchbook\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESmallhythe Place - an early 16th century half-timbered house that was home to renowned Victorian actress Ellen Terry from 1899 to 1928\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "23bf2805-8bdf-49f1-8802-1a6f53854434",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Hever Castle \u0026amp; Gardens\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 stop at a convenient property en route such as Hever Castle and Gardens, the childhood home of Anne Boleyn and dating back as far as 1270 \u2013 check in at the 3* Best Western Abbots Barton Hotel in Canterbury.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 Canterbury, Canterbury Cathedral \u0026amp; Leeds Castle\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGuided tour of the UNESCO listed city of Canterbury taking in the city walls \u2013 Canterbury Cathedral, dating back to 597AD when St Augustine established his seat in Canterbury, was the site of Archbishop Thomas Becket\u2019s murder in 1170 and ever since the Cathedral has attracted thousands of pilgrims, as told famously in Geoffrey Chaucer\u0026#39;s \u2018Canterbury Tales\u2019 \u2013 Leeds Castle, set in 500 acres of beautiful parkland and offering over 1,000 years of history, has Norman foundations, a medieval gatehouse, a Tudor tower and a 19th century country house, all of which were substantially refurbished in the 20th century by the last private owner of the castle, Lady Baillie, the heiress to an American fortune.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 Sissinghurst Castle Garden, Great Dixter House \u0026amp; All Saints\u2019 Church, Tudeley\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe National Trust\u2019s Sissinghurst Castle Garden is developed around the surviving parts of an Elizabethan mansion and provide outstanding design and colour throughout the season \u2013 Great Dixter House and Gardens was once the family home of the late Christopher Lloyd who devoted his life to creating one of the most experimental, exciting and constantly changing gardens of our time \u2013 All Saints\u2019 Church in Tudeley is internationally famous for its twelve stained glass windows by the great Russian artist Marc Chagall.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 Dover Castle \u0026amp; Walmer Castle\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EGuarding the Straits of Dover, English Heritage\u2019s Dover Castle occupies a site that has witnessed more than 2,000 years of history and its Secret Wartime Tunnels played an important role in World War II \u2013 English Heritage\u2019s Walmer Castle and Gardens was transformed from a Tudor castle into the elegant home and residence of the Lord Warden of the Cinque Ports.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 \u2013 Ightham Mote\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EStop at a convenient property en route home such as the National Trust\u2019s Ightham Mote, a superb moated manor house and garden dating from 1330 whose main features span many centuries and include the Great Hall and Tudor Chapel with painted ceiling \u2013 return to our original departure points with comfort stops en route.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        }
      ]
    },
